issues":3,"closed_issues":3687,"state":"closed","created_at":"2024-12-19T08:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T21:48:38Z","due_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-08-05T13:30:05Z","updated_at":"2025-08-07T18:18:41Z","closed_at":"2025-08-07T18:11:33Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.5.beta [45509c284cc8779f7e791b0d7dc3d639b3cc2fcc]\n- Not reproducible in: 4.4.1-stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta (45509c284) - Fedora Linux 42 (Adams) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 9070 XT (RADV GFX1201) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 60.39 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn short, because we now (as of #103403) actually output the progress log messages during `--headless --import`, similar to how `--headless --export` has worked for a long time, the logs will now be populated with all the resources that have been imported, like so:\n\n```\n[  45% ] reimport | some_resource.png\n```\n\nThis on its own is of course a very good thing. However, because the progress of these import tasks is being logged in a `while (true)` loop (assuming the default of `editor/import/use_multiple_threads`) while waiting for the import thread to do its thing, we can end up emitting _a lot_ of duplicate messages, which end up bloating the logs for no reason:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/c81fd6c51233a727da528cf7f74137d56b5d6efe/editor/file_system/editor_file_system.cpp#L3314-L3320\n\nSo in reality the logs for a single resource often look more like this:\n\n```\n[  45% ] reimport | some_resource.png\n[  45% ] reimport | some_resource.png\n[  45% ] reimport | some_resource.png\n[  45% ] reimport | some_resource.png\n[  45% ] reimport | some_resource.png\n[  45% ] reimport | some_resource.png\n[  45% ] reimport | some_resource.png\n...\n```\n\nThis can become annoying for larger projects with many/large resources, especially in a CI context like GitHub Actions that limits their log sizes, because the logs end up being hundreds of thousands of lines long:\n\n<img width=\"935\" height=\"28\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/31e94572-d786-4d05-b8b9-35813b2335f4\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Run `--headless --import` on any large project.\n2. Note the large amount of duplicate messages saying something like `[ ...% ] reimport | some_resource.png`.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThis relates to large-scale projects, so a minimal repro is not really applicable here.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109333/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":